    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The study of fracture localization is a first order problem for understanding the flow of fluids through reservoirs and aquifers. Joint clusters that are highly localized and restricted in length have been associated with faulting in field outcrops. This paper presents a new numerical model that simulates the localization of fault related opening-mode fractures along frictional faults. The clustering of secondary fractures produced by this frictional model, presents an exciting new application of BEM models and opens the door for future investigations of joint clustering within fractured reservoirs.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
